{{- /*
=============================================================================
dot_zprofile.tmpl → ~/.zprofile  (Homebrew login-shell PATH)

Replaces the `brew shellenv` injection block in install-mac.sh /
install-linux.sh. The path it writes previously lived in the install scripts
because `brew --prefix` is arch-conditional (/opt/homebrew, /usr/local, or
/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew). That division — install scripts own
machine-state-that-depends-on-runtime-values — no longer applies under
chezmoi, because templates evaluate `output` (or, here, `stat` on candidate
paths) at apply time on the actual target machine.

The template must NOT rely on `output "brew" "--prefix"` or `lookPath "brew"`
directly, because:
  • On a first apply against a fresh machine, `run_once_before_install-packages`
    installs Homebrew, but chezmoi's own process PATH is not updated for that
    session. `lookPath "brew"` would return empty EVEN IF brew was just
    installed by the preceding `before_` script.
  • `output "brew" "--prefix"` raises a template error if `brew` is not on
    PATH, which would break the apply.

Instead we `stat` the candidate brew install paths (Apple-Silicon, Intel,
Linux system, Linux user-prefix) and invoke the discovered brew binary via
its absolute path. `stat` returns false-y when the file doesn't exist and
structured data (truth-y) when it does — see chezmoi templates functions/stat
docs. This works on fresh installs (brew is on disk after the `before_`
install script runs) AND on existing installs, with zero OS branches.

On truly fresh machines where brew isn't installed yet (and the user runs
`chezmoi apply` without `init --apply`, skipping the install script), the
template renders to an empty file — a subsequent apply (after brew is
present) fills it in.
=============================================================================
*/ -}}
{{- $brew := "" -}}
{{- range $p := list "/opt/homebrew/bin/brew" "/usr/local/bin/brew" "/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin/brew" -}}
  {{- if stat $p -}}{{- $brew = $p -}}{{- end -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- if eq $brew "" -}}
  {{- $userbrew := joinPath .chezmoi.homeDir ".linuxbrew/bin/brew" -}}
  {{- if stat $userbrew -}}{{- $brew = $userbrew -}}{{- end -}}
{{- end -}}
# Added by dotfiles chezmoi template (.chezmoidata root → ~/.zprofile)
# Source shellenv so `brew` is on PATH for interactive zsh shells.
{{ if $brew -}}
eval "$({{ $brew }} shellenv)"
{{- end }}